# Property XoL v1 — coverage screening

A one-layer property excess-of-loss certificate. This file decides **coverage
only**; it never computes a ceded amount. Settlement is delegated to
`ReinsuranceLean`, whose `layerCeded` is the verified arithmetic.

Perils are classified by an exhaustive `match`, so adding a peril to the
enumeration is a compile error here until it has been classified. That is the
point: the wording must say what happens to every peril it names.

```catala
declaration scope Screen:
  input claim content Claim
  input terms content TreatyTerms
  output isCyber content boolean
  output isWar content boolean
  output isFlood content boolean
  output isEarthquake content boolean
  output verdict content Verdict

scope Screen:
  # Cl. 5.1 — cyber is excluded outright.
  definition isCyber equals
    match claim.peril with pattern
    -- Cyber : true
    -- Windstorm : false
    -- Flood : false
    -- Earthquake : false
    -- Fire : false
    -- War : false

  # Cl. 5.2 — war is excluded outright.
  definition isWar equals
    match claim.peril with pattern
    -- War : true
    -- Windstorm : false
    -- Flood : false
    -- Earthquake : false
    -- Fire : false
    -- Cyber : false

  # Cl. 4.2 — flood is excluded only when the schedule says so.
  definition isFlood equals
    match claim.peril with pattern
    -- Flood : true
    -- Windstorm : false
    -- Earthquake : false
    -- Fire : false
    -- Cyber : false
    -- War : false

  # Cl. 4.2 — earthquake is excluded only when the schedule says so.
  definition isEarthquake equals
    match claim.peril with pattern
    -- Earthquake : true
    -- Windstorm : false
    -- Flood : false
    -- Fire : false
    -- Cyber : false
    -- War : false

  # Clause order follows the wording: period, absolute exclusions, scheduled
  # exclusions, certification, cover.
  definition verdict equals
    if claim.incidentDay < terms.inceptionDay
       or claim.incidentDay > terms.expiryDay then
      Verdict {
        -- kind : Excluded
        -- citedClauses : [Cl_6_1_TreatyPeriod]
        -- pending : []
      }
    else if isCyber then
      Verdict {
        -- kind : Excluded
        -- citedClauses : [Cl_5_1_CyberExclusion]
        -- pending : []
      }
    else if isWar then
      Verdict {
        -- kind : Excluded
        -- citedClauses : [Cl_5_2_WarExclusion]
        -- pending : []
      }
    else if (isFlood and terms.excludesFlood)
         or (isEarthquake and terms.excludesEarthquake) then
      Verdict {
        -- kind : Excluded
        -- citedClauses : [Cl_4_2_PerilExclusion]
        -- pending : []
      }
    else if not claim.isCertified then
      Verdict {
        -- kind : Incomplete
        -- citedClauses : [Cl_7_3_Certification]
        -- pending : [AdjusterCertification]
      }
    # Cl. 7.4 — an unresolved court ruling does not pay cash; it books a reserve.
    else if not claim.litigationFinal then
      Verdict {
        -- kind : Reserved
        -- citedClauses : [Cl_4_1_PerilsInsured; Cl_8_1_LimitAndRetention; Cl_7_4_UnresolvedCourtRulingReserve]
        -- pending : []
      }
    else
      Verdict {
        -- kind : Covered
        -- citedClauses : [Cl_4_1_PerilsInsured; Cl_8_1_LimitAndRetention]
        -- pending : []
      }
```
